-- title:
--   T_ℓ on mod p differentials matches T_ℓ on cusp forms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup such that every unit $u$ with $\mathrm{unitsMap}\,u = 1$ under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ lies in $H$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ given by the lower right entry. Assume $f$ lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every $t$ in the Hecke ring `heckeRingH` (the subring generated by the range of `heckeGenH` for the empty set of excluded primes in weight $2$), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $M$ at $p$ and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-coefficient of $t f$ and of the weight-$2$ Atkin–Lehner slash `alSlash W 2` of $t f$ lie in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$. Let $pf \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ satisfy `IsIntegralQExp f pf`, i.e. the image of $pf$ in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion of $f$ of width $1$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid M$ and let $p\ell f \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ be an integral $q$-expansion in the same sense of [`CuspForm.heckeTLinH 2 hℓ hℓM f`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L224), the operator which, when the stability predicate `StableT M H 2 ℓ` holds, sends $g$ to $\mathrm{heckeU}_{2,\ell}\,g$ plus the weight-$2$ slash of $g$ by the lift of the unit attached to $\ell$ times `heckeDiagMatrix ℓ`, and is $0$ otherwise. Write $N = M/p$ and $H'=$ `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, and let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH N H')` be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the ratios `intFormRatiosC`. Let $\omega \in \Omega[F/K]$ be such that `diffQExp F ω`, the $K((q))$-valued map on Kähler differentials obtained from the $q$-Euler derivation `qEulerOn F`, equals `intSeriesC K pf`, the Laurent series image of $pf$ under $\mathbb{Z} \to K$. Then `diffQExp F` applied to `heckeDiffModLH K N H' ℓ ω`, the correspondence given by pull-back along `heckeAlphaModLH` followed by the trace along `heckeBetaModLH`, equals `intSeriesC K pℓf`.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion form of the statement that the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$, for a prime $\ell$ not dividing $M$, acts on differentials of the characteristic-$p$ $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H'}(M/p)$ exactly as $T_\ell$ acts on two-cusp integral weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_H(M)$; the companion statement for the diamond operators is [`ModularCurve.diffQExp_diamondDiffModLH_eq_intSeriesC_of_diffQExp_eq_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.diffQExp_diamondDiffModLH_eq_intSeriesC_of_diffQExp_eq_of_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet). It is used in [`ModularCurve.IsInfReductionMap.comp_baseChange_genT_eq_genDiffModL_comp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IsInfReductionMap.comp_baseChange_genT_eq_genDiffModL_comp) to identify the Hecke action on the reduction at the component through $\infty$ with the Hecke action on differentials.
